Abstract = {The history of the development of Taxol (R) (paclitaxel) as an
   anticancer drug is reviewed, and some aspects of the phytochemistry of
   Taxus species and of the medicinal chemistry of taxol are discussed. The
   nature of the taxol-tubulin interaction is then described, with an
   emphasis on studies that led to the discovery and experimental proof of
   the T-taxol conformation as the tubulin-binding conformation of taxol.
